Two tables merged into one: `meal` is made @from `lunch`, and `dinner`'s
rows can only be dropped on purpose (copied first). Rows from both need a
task in `init!`, or data migrations in Roc: an @from makes a table from
one other, never two.

== before
CREATE TABLE lunch (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE dinner (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO lunch VALUES (1, 'soup');
INSERT INTO dinner VALUES (1, 'roast');

== after
-- @release 1
-- @drop 1 table lunch
-- @from 1 table meal = lunch
-- @drop 1 table dinner
CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 5 steps
  table `dinner`: dropped on purpose
    DROP TABLE "dinner"
  table `meal`: `lunch` aside, to make it from
    ALTER TABLE "lunch" RENAME TO "roux_old_lunch"
  table `meal`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT
  table `meal`: its rows, by id, title
    INSERT INTO "meal" ("id", "title") SELECT "id", "title" FROM "roux_old_lunch"
  table `meal`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_lunch"
migrated from release 0
